{"id":"h131","run":2,"role":"calibration","category":"claim","question":"Is the following claim true? The Danube flows into the Adriatic Sea.","truth":"no","model_answer":"no","correct":true,"source":"author-written for this project; verified by the author","claims":[{"text":"The Danube is one of Europe's major rivers.","confidence":0.95,"lean":0.0,"theta":1.4923,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The Danube flows through countries bordering the Adriatic region, such as Croatia and Serbia.","confidence":0.6,"lean":1,"theta":0.9425,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The Sava, flowing through Croatia and Bosnia, joins the Danube at Belgrade.","confidence":0.9,"lean":0.0,"theta":1.4137,"phi":0.0},{"text":"Tributary links to the Adriatic region make the claim seem plausible at first glance.","confidence":0.4,"lean":1,"theta":0.6283,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The Danube's mouth is in the Danube Delta on the Romanian coast.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The Danube empties into the Black Sea, not the Adriatic.","confidence":0.98,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5394,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The Danube runs east through Central and Southeastern Europe and never reaches the Adriatic.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The Adriatic is fed by other rivers such as the Po, Adige, and Neretva.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Proximity of some tributaries to the Adriatic basin does not change where the Danube drains.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The claim that the Danube flows into the Adriatic is false.","confidence":0.98,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5394,"phi":-3.1416}],"relations":[{"i":1,"j":2,"J":0.3,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":3,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":5,"J":-0.4,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":1,"j":6,"J":-0.5,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":1,"j":8,"J":-0.3,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":1,"j":9,"J":-0.3,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":2,"j":3,"J":0.3,"relation":"suppor